Enable quantized TFLite models in the Relax TFLite frontend (TVM 0.25).

Three independent fixes, needed to convert a full-integer-quantized model:

1. _SUPPORTED_QUANTIZED_OPS is missing six operators that the frontend already
   implements correctly for quantized input:

   - MAX_POOL_2D, PAD, RESIZE_NEAREST_NEIGHBOR, STRIDED_SLICE, TRANSPOSE only move
     elements around — no arithmetic on the values — and TFLite gives their input and
     output the same quantization params, so they run unchanged on int8. RESHAPE and
     RESIZE_BILINEAR, the same class of op, were already on the list.
   - AVERAGE_POOL_2D does do arithmetic, but convert_pool2d already has a proper
     quantized path: it casts to int32 to accumulate without overflow, averages, and
     casts back, guarded by an assert that input and output share scale and zero
     point — exactly the condition under which averaging quantized values equals
     averaging the reals.

   In every case the converter code exists and the op is simply absent from the
   allowlist, so it is rejected before it is ever reached.

2. The quantize/dequantize helpers forward qnn_params["axis"] to relax.op.quantize /
   relax.op.dequantize, which validate 0 <= axis <= ndim-1. A 0-d scalar operand
   (e.g. the quantized scalar constant feeding a MUL in YOLOv8) has no valid axis and
   the build dies with "axis param is out of range (0)". Lift such operands to rank 1
   for the QDQ call and squeeze them back. Independent of (1): it also fires on ops
   that were already on the allowlist.

3. convert_pool2d's quantized average path and the FLOAT16 branch call relax.op.cast
   and relax.cast, neither of which exists in TVM 0.25 (the op is relax.op.astype).
   That is dead code today: the pool path is unreachable while AVERAGE_POOL_2D is off
   the allowlist, so enabling (1) exposes it. Fixing it also unbreaks float16 models,
   which failed with "module 'tvm.relax' has no attribute 'cast'".

Validated on yolov8n full_integer_quant.tflite: 256/256 ops converted, model.so built,
inference returns "person" at 0.877 confidence (a broken QDQ lowering returns noise).
AVERAGE_POOL_2D was added later for a yolov8-pose model that needs it.

Not covered: dynamic-range quantization is rejected earlier by a separate check and
that rejection is correct (activation scales are computed at run time and are not in
the file); float16 fails elsewhere on a missing relax.cast.

--- a/tvm/relax/frontend/tflite/tflite_frontend.py
